  triage:closedBy "team-lead" ;
  triage:closureNote "Independently verified via git show ac465283747d3186667fab7ad2f752b1c4c1a968 -- crates/atm-daemon/src/https_transport.rs: new test advertised_ip_peer_write_uses_real_dispatcher_persists_and_nudges (line ~983) uses a real DaemonRequestDispatcher (not RecordingRouter mock), real SQLite-backed persistence (dispatcher.dispatch(Receive) confirms the persisted recipient record), and a real socket-based GraftReceiverListener nudge round trip for both the peer write and the canonical ACK. This satisfies the sprint doc's real-adapter/persistence/nudge requirement. The pre-existing mocked advertised_ip_peer_send_and_ack_reach_the_shared_router test at line ~1358 is left in place as a separate lower-level transport-routing check, not as the ACK proof." ;
